s asked you for advice. They are shopping for a pair of wireless earbuds and are torn between the options shown below. Here is what they told you, in their own words:\n\n\"I'm looking for a pair of wireless earbuds. I care about an open-ear or ear-hook design, an IPX8 submersion waterproof rating, and at least 12 hours of playback per charge. Which of these should I get?\""}, {"Description": "table_html", "Type": "Custom", "Field": "table_html", "VariableType": "String", "DataVisibility": [], "AnalyzeText": false, "Value": "<style>.sb-table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;max-width:920px;margin:0 auto;font-size:14px;color:#1a1a1a}.sb-table th,.sb-table td{border:1px solid #cfd6dd;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}.sb-table thead th{background:#f4f6f8}.sb-prod{font-weight:700}.sb-model{font-weight:400;color:#566;font-size:12px}.sb-row{background:#fafbfc;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap}.sb-parity td{color:#444}</style><table class='sb-table'><thead><tr><th></th><th class='sb-prod'>Vynex<div class='sb-model'>OpenReal</div></th><th class='sb-prod'>Shokz<div class='sb-model'>OpenRun Pro 2</div></th><th class='sb-prod'>Beats<div class='sb-model'>Fit Pro</div></th><th class='sb-prod'>JBL<div class='sb-model'>Endurance Race</div></th><th class='sb-prod'>Sony<div class='sb-model'>WF-SP800N</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th class='sb-row'>Price</th><td>$39.99</td><td>$179.99</td><td>$159.99</td><td>$49.99</td><td>$129.99</td></tr><tr><th class='sb-row'>Fit / design</th><td>ear-hook open</td><td>bone conduction</td><td>wingtip</td><td>twistlock</td><td>arc support</td></tr><tr><th class='sb-row'>Battery life</th><td>14h (48h case)</td><td>12h</td><td>6h (27h case)</td><td>10h (30h case)</td><td>9h (18h case)</td></tr><tr><th class='sb-row'>Audio codec</th><td>AAC/SBC</td><td>SBC</td><td>AAC</td><td>AAC/SBC</td><td>AAC/SBC</td></tr><tr><th class='sb-row'>Water rating</th><td>IPX8</td><td>IP55</td><td>IPX4</td><td>IP67</td><td>IP55</td></tr><tr class='sb-parity'><th class='sb-row'>Customer rating</th><td>4.3 / 5 average customer rating</td><td>4.3 / 5 average customer rating</td><td>4.3 / 5 average customer rating</td><td>4.3 / 5 average customer rating</td><td>4.3 / 5 average customer rating</td></tr><tr class='sb-parity'><th class='sb-row'>Number of reviews</th><td>500 verified reviews</td><td>500 verified reviews</td><td>500 verified reviews</td><td>500 verified reviews</td><td>500 verified reviews</td></tr></tbody></table>"}, {"Description": "glossary_full", "Type": "Custom", "Field": "glossary_full", "VariableType": "String", "DataVisibility": [], "AnalyzeText": false, "Value": "<div style='max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:16px 20px;background:#f6f8fa;border:1px solid #e1e4e8;border-radius:10px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#222'><div style='font-weight:700;font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px'>What these product specs mean</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;color:#555;font-size:14px'>Please read these before you choose. On the next screen you will compare the products and make one choice; a short reminder of these definitions stays available there.</div><ul style='margin:0;padding-left:20px'><li style='margin:.5em 0'><b>Battery life:</b> how long it runs on one charge (in hours, or mAh capacity for phones); higher is better.</li><li style='margin:.5em 0'><b>Water rating (IP / IPX):</b> protection against water; a higher number means more protection (IPX8 survives brief submersion; IP67 is dust- and water-resistant).</li></ul></div>"}, {"Description": "glossary_compact", "Type": "Custom", "Field": "glossary_compact", "VariableType": "String", "DataVisibility": [], "AnalyzeText": false, "Value": "<details class='sb-gloss' style='max-width:760px;margin:12px auto 0;padding:8px 14px;background:#f6f8fa;border:1px solid #e1e4e8;border-radius:8px;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.5;color:#333'><summary style='cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;color:#444'>What these terms mean (reminder)</summary><ul style='mar